{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "Expand / zoom out video (Wan2.2 Fun VACE)",
    "description": "Core nodes only. Video outpainting: the first 81 source frames (VideoTemporalCrop, native fps) are scaled into the centre of a ~480p VACE canvas and padded with neutral grey (ImagePadForOutpaint); the pad mask, repeated per frame, is the only area WanVaceToVideo generates. Two-stage Wan2.2 sampling as vace_reframe (balanced: high-noise without LoRA cfg 3.5 steps 0-4, low-noise + lightx2v cfg 1; fast: LoRA both, 4 steps). The decode is trimmed back to the source frame count, upscaled to the expanded output size, and the ORIGINAL frames are composited back over the centre (ImageCompositeMasked) with a mask that is 1.0 everywhere except a few-px FeatherMask ramp along the padded edges only, so source pixels are unchanged. Source fps and audio (GetVideoComponents) are passed to CreateVideo. The builder (src/lib/oj/videoExpand.ts) sets canvas, pads, feather and the size expressions; everything that depends on the real decoded frame size is computed in-graph from GetImageSize (ComfyMathExpression): node 23 fits the source (even size, expanded frame <= 2560 px; identity for normal clips), nodes 48 (fitted size), 42/43 give the output size and 44/45 the paste-back offsets, so a run with a wrong recorded width/height still pastes back in place."
  },
